package com.prayerkey.manna.data

import com.prayerkey.manna.resources.*

/*
 * More reading plans, in the same shape as ReadingPlansData.kt. Each day is a
 * short passage, a devotion on it, a prayer point and a question. The key
 * verse on each plan is the King James text, word for word. One val per plan
 * so no single initializer outgrows a JVM method.
 */

private val MORE_0 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "grief-and-loss",
    title = "Grief and Loss",
    topic = "Healing",
    blurb = "Seven days for the weeks after a loss, when the house is quiet and people have stopped calling.",
    verse = "The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 34:18",
    art = Res.drawable.rhythm_evening,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Jesus Wept", "John", 11, 32, 44, "He Cried Too", "Jesus knew He was about to raise Lazarus, and still He stood at the grave and wept. Your tears are not a failure of faith. They are love with nowhere left to go. The Lord does not hurry you past your grief or tell you to be strong. He comes and stands in it with you, and He is not ashamed to cry.", "Tell God plainly who you have lost and what you miss most.", "What would you say to Jesus if He stood beside you at the grave?"),
        PlanDay("Close to the Broken", "Psalms", 34, 15, 22, "Nigh unto Them", "Grief can make God feel far away, as if prayer hits the ceiling and falls back. This psalm says the opposite. The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart. You do not have to feel Him for Him to be near. He hears the cry you cannot put into words, and He keeps you even when you cannot keep yourself.", "Ask God to make His nearness real to you today, even in small ways.", "Where have you felt most alone since your loss?"),
        PlanDay("A Time to Mourn", "Ecclesiastes", 3, 1, 8, "There Is a Season", "Scripture makes room for mourning. There is a time to weep, and it is not something to rush or hide. Some people will expect you to be better by now. God does not keep that kind of clock. The season of mourning is real, and so is the season after it. You are allowed to be where you are.", "Ask God for patience with yourself in this season.", "Who has expected you to move on faster than you can?"),
        PlanDay("A Place Prepared", "John", 14, 1, 6, "In My Father's House", "Jesus spoke these words to friends who were about to lose Him. He did not deny the sorrow coming. He gave them something to hold: a house with many rooms, and a promise that He would come again for them. For those who die in Christ, death is not the end of the story. It is a door He has already walked through.", "Thank God for the hope of His house, and for every loved one who rests in Christ.", "What part of this promise do you most need to hold on to?"),
        PlanDay("Grieving with Hope", "1 Thessalonians", 4, 13, 18, "Not as Others", "Paul does not tell believers not to grieve. He tells them not to grieve as those who have no hope. Christian grief still hurts, but it is not hopeless. Jesus died and rose again, and those who sleep in Him will rise too. Paul ends by saying, comfort one another with these words. Hope is meant to be shared aloud.", "Ask God to hold your sorrow and your hope together.", "Who could you share this hope with this week?"),
        PlanDay("Comfort Passed On", "2 Corinthians", 1, 3, 7, "The God of All Comfort", "God comforts us in all our trouble, and one day that comfort becomes something we can give to others. That day may not be today. For now, it is enough to receive. But nothing you are walking through is wasted. The comfort you are given in this valley will one day reach someone else who is standing where you stand now.", "Ask God to comfort you, and to send you people who know how to sit with you.", "Who has comforted you well, and what did they do?"),
        PlanDay("Every Tear Wiped Away", "Revelation", 7, 13, 17, "No More Tears", "This is where the story is going. A day is coming when the Lamb will lead His people to living waters, and God Himself will wipe away all tears from their eyes. He does not ignore the tears; He wipes them away, one by one. Until that day, every tear you cry is seen. None of them are lost on Him.", "Thank God for the day when grief will be no more.", "How does the end of the story change the way you carry today?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_1 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "marriage",
    title = "Marriage",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Seven days of Scripture for husbands and wives, whether newly married or many years in.",
    verse = "And if one prevail against him, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.",
    verseRef = "Ecclesiastes 4:12",
    art = Res.drawable.onboarding_church_v3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Not Good to Be Alone", "Genesis", 2, 18, 25, "Made for Each Other", "Before there was sin in the world, God looked at the man alone and said it was not good. Marriage was His idea, not a human arrangement. He brought the woman to the man as a gift. When marriage feels like hard work, it helps to remember where it began: in the heart of a God who delights to give good things.", "Thank God for your spouse by name, and for one thing you saw in them at the start.", "What first drew you to the person you married?"),
        PlanDay("Love Suffereth Long", "1 Corinthians", 13, 4, 8, "What Love Does", "The KJV calls it charity, and it is love that acts. It is patient and kind. It does not keep score. Read slowly, this passage is less a poem and more a mirror. Few of us measure up for long. The good news is that this is how God loves us, and He is able to grow the same love in us.", "Ask God to grow one of these marks of love in you this week.", "Which line in this passage is hardest for you to live out at home?"),
        PlanDay("One Flesh", "Ephesians", 5, 21, 33, "Submitting One to Another", "Paul begins with a word to both husband and wife: Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God. Then he points husbands to the cross: Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it. Marriage at its best is two people each laying down their own way for the good of the other, with Christ at the centre.", "Ask God to show you one way to put your spouse first today.", "Where are you holding on to your own way at home?"),
        PlanDay("Bear with One Another", "Colossians", 3, 12, 15, "Forgiving", "Every marriage is two forgiven sinners living under one roof. There will be things to forgive, some small and some not. Paul says to put on mercy, kindness and patience like clothes, and to forgive as Christ forgave you. Forgiveness does not pretend the hurt never happened. It chooses not to keep it as a weapon.", "Bring to God anything you are still holding against your spouse.", "Is there an old hurt that still comes up in your arguments?"),
        PlanDay("A Threefold Cord", "Ecclesiastes", 4, 9, 12, "Two Are Better", "Two people can lift each other up when one falls. But the passage ends with three strands, not two. A marriage held only by the strength of two people can fray. A marriage where both turn to God together has a third strand that does not break easily. Praying together, even briefly, is one of the strongest things a couple can do.", "Pray with your spouse today, even if it is one sentence each.", "What makes it hard for the two of you to pray together?"),
        PlanDay("Prayers Not Hindered", "1 Peter", 3, 7, 12, "Heirs Together", "Peter tells husbands to honour their wives as heirs together of the grace of life, so that their prayers are not hindered. How we treat each other at home is connected to how we pray. He goes on to say, be pitiful, be courteous, and do not return insult for insult. Kindness in the house opens the way for prayer.", "Ask God to make your words at home gentle and honest.", "How has the way you speak at home affected your prayers?"),
        PlanDay("Love That Lasts", "Song of Solomon", 8, 5, 7, "Many Waters", "Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it. Every marriage meets floods: money troubles, illness, children, disappointment, long seasons of being tired. Love that is rooted in God can come through them. It may look different at fifty than it did at twenty-five, but it can be deeper, not weaker. Ask Him to keep the fire burning.", "Ask God to protect your marriage and renew your love for each other.", "What is one thing you could do this week to show your spouse love?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_2 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "parenting",
    title = "Parenting",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Seven days for mothers, fathers and anyone raising a child, on the hard and holy work of it.",
    verse = "Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.",
    verseRef = "Proverbs 22:6",
    art = Res.drawable.verse_card_botanical,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("At Home and on the Way", "Deuteronomy", 6, 4, 9, "Talk of Them", "God did not give faith to Israel's children through a weekly lesson alone. He told parents to speak of His words when they sat in the house, walked by the way, lay down and rose up. Faith is passed on in ordinary moments: the school run, the dinner table, bedtime. Your children learn most from what you love when nobody is watching.", "Ask God to show you one ordinary moment today to speak of Him with your child.", "When do your children hear you talk about God?"),
        PlanDay("A Heritage from the LORD", "Psalms", 127, 1, 5, "Children Are a Gift", "Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it. Parents carry a great deal, and much of it is out of our control. This psalm takes some of the weight off. Your children are a heritage from the Lord, not a project you must perfect alone. You can work hard and still rest, because He is the builder.", "Give each of your children back to God by name.", "What worry about your child do you need to hand to God?"),
        PlanDay("Lent to the LORD", "1 Samuel", 1, 24, 28, "Hannah's Gift", "Hannah had prayed for years for a son. When Samuel came, she brought him to the Lord and said, as long as he liveth he shall be lent to the LORD. Every parent must learn this slowly: our children belong to God before they belong to us. Letting go a little at a time is painful, but it is also an act of faith.", "Pray that your children would know God for themselves.", "Where are you finding it hard to let your child grow up?"),
        PlanDay("Provoke Not Your Children", "Ephesians", 6, 1, 4, "Nurture and Admonition", "Children are told to honour their parents. Fathers, and all parents with them, are told, provoke not your children to wrath. Discipline matters, but so does the way it is given. Harshness can teach a child that God is harsh. Patience, fairness and warmth teach them something truer. Children forgive a great deal from a parent who says sorry.", "Ask God for patience in the moments when you are most likely to lose your temper.", "Is there anything you need to apologise to your child for?"),
        PlanDay("The Father Ran", "Luke", 15, 11, 24, "While He Was Yet a Great Way Off", "The father in this story watched the road. When he saw his son a long way off, he ran to him. Some parents are praying for a child who has wandered from home or from faith. This story is for you. God is that kind of Father, and He has not stopped watching the road for your child either. Keep praying.", "Pray for any child, yours or another, who has wandered from God.", "Which child is God asking you to keep praying for?"),
        PlanDay("Let the Children Come", "Mark", 10, 13, 16, "Suffer the Little Children", "The disciples thought the children were in the way. Jesus was much displeased, took them up in His arms and blessed them. Children are not too young to be loved by Jesus or to pray to Him. Bring them to Him often, in simple ways. Bless them out loud. They will remember being blessed long after they forget the words.", "Lay your hand on your child and speak a blessing over them today.", "How could you help your children feel welcome with Jesus?"),
        PlanDay("Unfeigned Faith", "2 Timothy", 1, 3, 7, "Lois and Eunice", "Timothy's faith had lived first in his grandmother Lois and his mother Eunice. Paul does not mention great sermons. He mentions faith that was real, lived out at home. You may feel you have little to give your children. Real faith, honest prayer and a life that matches your words is enough to plant something that lasts for generations.", "Thank God for those who passed faith on to you, and ask Him to help you do the same.", "Who planted faith in you, and how did they do it?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_3 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "waiting-on-god",
    title = "Waiting on God",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Seven days for when the answer has not come yet and you are tired of waiting.",
    verse = "But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.",
    verseRef = "Isaiah 40:31",
    art = Res.drawable.verse_card_dawn,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Wait on the LORD", "Psalms", 27, 7, 14, "Be of Good Courage", "David ends this psalm by telling himself what to do: Wait on the LORD: be of good courage. Waiting is not doing nothing. It is choosing, again and again, to keep looking to God rather than giving up or running ahead. Courage is needed for it. Some of the bravest people you know are simply people who have kept on waiting well.", "Tell God honestly how long you have been waiting and how you feel about it.", "What are you waiting for God to do?"),
        PlanDay("I Waited Patiently", "Psalms", 40, 1, 5, "He Inclined unto Me", "David waited patiently, and the Lord inclined to him and heard his cry. Before the answer came, there was a pit, miry clay and a long wait. The psalm does not skip that part. But it ends with a new song and feet on a rock. What God did for David, He is able to do for you, in His time.", "Ask God to lift you out of whatever pit you are in, and to give you patience until He does.", "What would your new song be if this prayer were answered?"),
        PlanDay("Though It Tarry", "Habakkuk", 2, 1, 4, "The Vision Is for an Appointed Time", "Habakkuk climbed his watchtower to see what God would say. The answer was: write it down, because it is for an appointed time. though it tarry, wait for it. Some promises take longer than we want. Delay is not the same as denial. The just shall live by faith, and faith is what holds on in the gap.", "Write down what you believe God has promised you, and pray over it.", "What has God said that you are still waiting to see?"),
        PlanDay("At the Set Time", "Genesis", 21, 1, 7, "Sarah Laughed", "Sarah had laughed when she heard she would have a son in her old age. It sounded impossible. Then the LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and she bore a son at the set time. God's timing rarely matches ours, but He is never late on His own calendar. Sarah's laughter of doubt became laughter of joy.", "Ask God to turn your doubt into joy in His time.", "Where have you stopped expecting God to act?"),
        PlanDay("More Than the Watchmen", "Psalms", 130, 1, 8, "My Soul Waiteth", "The watchman on the city wall waits for morning because he knows it will come. He cannot make the sun rise faster, but he is sure of it. The psalmist waits for the Lord like that. You may be in the dark part of the night right now. Morning is still coming. The God who forgives is the God who keeps His word.", "Thank God that the morning will come, even if you cannot see it yet.", "What helps you keep hoping when the night feels long?"),
        PlanDay("For Him That Waiteth", "Isaiah", 64, 1, 5, "What He Hath Prepared", "Isaiah prays for God to come down and act. Then he remembers that since the world began, no eye has seen a God like this, one who has prepared such things for him that waiteth for him. Your waiting is not wasted time. God is at work while you wait, in your situation and in you, in ways you may only see later.", "Ask God to show you what He is doing in you while you wait.", "How has waiting changed you so far?"),
        PlanDay("Hope That Is Not Seen", "Romans", 8, 18, 25, "With Patience Wait", "Paul says the whole creation groans while it waits, and so do we. Hope that is seen is not hope. If you already had it, you would not need to wait. Waiting with hope means living today as someone sure of tomorrow. The glory coming is so great that Paul calls our present sufferings not worthy to be compared with it.", "Ask God for hope that is strong enough to carry you through the wait.", "What does it look like to wait with hope rather than with dread?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_4 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "forgiveness",
    title = "Forgiveness",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Seven days on being forgiven by God, and finding the grace to forgive others.",
    verse = "And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you.",
    verseRef = "Ephesians 4:32",
    art = Res.drawable.verse_card_oxblood,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("The Blessed Man", "Psalms", 32, 1, 7, "When I Kept Silence", "David knew what it was to carry unconfessed sin. When he kept silent, his bones waxed old and his strength dried up. When he confessed, God forgave. Hiding is heavy. Confession is not God collecting evidence against you; it is the door He opens to set you free. Blessed is the one whose sin is covered by Him.", "Confess to God anything you have been carrying alone.", "What have you been keeping silent about before God?"),
        PlanDay("White as Snow", "Isaiah", 1, 16, 18, "Come Now, and Let Us Reason", "God invites His people to come and reason with Him. though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow. Nothing you have done is too dark for Him to wash. You may struggle to forgive yourself. Begin by believing what He says about your sin once it is confessed: it is washed, and He does not hold it against you.", "Thank God that your sins are washed white.", "Is there something you have confessed that you still feel guilty about?"),
        PlanDay("She Loved Much", "Luke", 7, 40, 48, "Forgiven Much", "A woman known for her sins wept at Jesus' feet while a religious man looked down on her. Jesus said that the one who is forgiven much loves much. The more we understand what we have been forgiven, the more we love, and the easier it becomes to forgive others. Forgiven people make forgiving people.", "Thank Jesus for how much He has forgiven you.", "How does remembering your own forgiveness change how you see others?"),
        PlanDay("Father, Forgive Them", "Luke", 23, 33, 38, "From the Cross", "While they were mocking Him, Jesus prayed, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do. He did not wait for an apology. Forgiveness began in His heart while the wound was still being made. We are not Jesus, and forgiving a deep hurt can take time. But His prayer shows us where the road leads.", "Pray for someone who has hurt you, even if all you can say is their name.", "Who is the hardest person for you to forgive right now?"),
        PlanDay("When Ye Stand Praying", "Mark", 11, 22, 26, "Forgive", "Jesus connected prayer and forgiveness. when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any. Unforgiveness is like a stone in the shoe of our prayer life. It does not stop God from loving us, but it keeps us from walking freely with Him. Forgiving is not saying the wrong was fine. It is handing the debt to God.", "Name before God what you are holding against someone, and hand it to Him.", "What would it cost you to let this go?"),
        PlanDay("Esau Ran to Meet Him", "Genesis", 33, 1, 4, "Reconciled", "Jacob had cheated his brother and fled. Twenty years later he came home terrified. Esau ran to meet him, and embraced him, and fell on his neck, and kissed him: and they wept. Not every story ends this way. Sometimes the other person does not want peace. But sometimes God has been softening a heart for years, and reconciliation is closer than you think.", "Ask God whether there is a relationship He wants you to try to mend.", "Is there someone you need to reach out to?"),
        PlanDay("Tenderhearted", "Ephesians", 4, 29, 32, "As God for Christ's Sake", "Paul gives a simple pattern: be kind, be tenderhearted, forgive, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you. We forgive because we have been forgiven, and in the same way. Not by pretending, but by grace. Bitterness keeps the wound open. Forgiveness lets it begin to heal. It may take many prayers, but God is patient with us.", "Ask God to replace any bitterness in you with kindness.", "What would being tenderhearted look like toward someone who hurt you?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_5 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "anxious-nights",
    title = "Peace for Anxious Nights",
    topic = "Peace",
    blurb = "Seven short readings for the end of the day, when your mind will not stop and sleep will not come.",
    verse = "I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 4:8",
    art = Res.drawable.today_prayer_violet,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("I Will Lay Me Down", "Psalms", 4, 1, 8, "Commune with Your Own Heart", "David wrote this at the end of a hard day. He tells himself to commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still, and he ends with a quiet decision: I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep. Sleep is an act of trust. You are not the one keeping the world turning tonight. The Lord is, and He makes you dwell in safety.", "Hand God each worry from today, one at a time, before you sleep.", "What is keeping you awake tonight?"),
        PlanDay("I Laid Me Down and Slept", "Psalms", 3, 1, 6, "A Shield for Me", "David wrote this psalm while running from his own son. Enemies were many, and people said God would not help him. Yet he says, I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me. If David could sleep in that, you can rest tonight. The Lord is a shield around you, and He will sustain you till morning.", "Ask God to be your shield through the night.", "What voices tell you God will not help you?"),
        PlanDay("He Will Not Slumber", "Psalms", 121, 1, 8, "Your Keeper", "You need sleep. God does not. he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep. While you rest, He is awake. He keeps your going out and your coming in. You can close your eyes because Someone else is keeping watch over you, your family and everything you are worried about. Let Him do the watching tonight.", "Give God the night watch over your home and the people you love.", "What do you find hardest to stop watching over yourself?"),
        PlanDay("Asleep in the Ship", "Matthew", 8, 23, 27, "A Great Calm", "The storm was so bad that experienced fishermen thought they would die. Jesus was asleep. When they woke Him, He spoke to the wind and there was a great calm. The same Jesus is with you tonight. He is not panicking about what you are facing. He is able to speak calm into the storm outside and the storm inside you.", "Ask Jesus to speak peace to the storm in your mind.", "What storm do you need Jesus to calm?"),
        PlanDay("Thy Sleep Shall Be Sweet", "Proverbs", 3, 21, 26, "Thou Shalt Not Be Afraid", "When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet. This promise is given to those who keep God's wisdom close. Sudden fear and the troubles of tomorrow do not have the final word. the LORD shall be thy confidence. Before you sleep, put your confidence back where it belongs.", "Ask God for sweet sleep and for confidence in Him.", "What sudden fear tends to come at night for you?"),
        PlanDay("The Terror by Night", "Psalms", 91, 1, 6, "Under His Wings", "Night can magnify every fear. Problems that looked manageable at noon look huge at two in the morning. This psalm speaks to that: Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night. Picture a bird covering her young under her wings. That is how near and how safe God means you to be as you rest under His shadow.", "Rest under God's wings tonight, and tell Him what frightens you.", "What feels bigger at night than it does in the day?"),
        PlanDay("In the Night Watches", "Psalms", 63, 1, 8, "I Remember Thee upon My Bed", "Sometimes sleep does not come. David knew those nights too. Instead of fighting them, he used them to remember God and meditate on Him in the night watches. If you lie awake, you do not have to fill the hours with worry. Let them become a quiet time with the Lord. His right hand holds you, even in the dark.", "If you wake tonight, turn the time into quiet prayer.", "What is one thing about God you could think on when you cannot sleep?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_6 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "morning-with-god",
    title = "Starting Your Day with God",
    topic = "Prayer",
    blurb = "Five mornings to build the habit of meeting God before the day begins.",
    verse = "My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct my prayer unto thee, and will look up.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 5:3",
    art = Res.drawable.rhythm_morning,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("In the Morning", "Psalms", 5, 1, 8, "I Will Direct My Prayer", "David says, in the morning will I direct my prayer unto thee, and will look up. He prays and then watches for God's answer through the day. A morning prayer does not have to be long. It is a way of saying, before anyone else gets my attention today, You have it. Then you look up, expecting Him to be at work.", "Give God the first few minutes of your day, before your phone.", "What usually gets your attention first in the morning?"),
        PlanDay("A Great While Before Day", "Mark", 1, 32, 39, "Jesus Rose Early", "The night before had been full of crowds and healing. Jesus must have been tired. Yet a great while before day He went out to a solitary place and prayed. If Jesus needed time alone with the Father, so do we. Find your solitary place: a chair, a corner, a walk. It need not be early, but it needs to be yours.", "Ask God to help you find a quiet place and time to meet Him.", "Where could your solitary place be?"),
        PlanDay("Thy Lovingkindness in the Morning", "Psalms", 92, 1, 5, "It Is a Good Thing", "It is a good thing to give thanks unto the LORD, and to shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning. Starting with thanks changes how a day begins. Before you list what you need, name what He has already given: breath, a new day, His mercy. Thanks turns your face toward God before the day pulls it elsewhere.", "Begin today by thanking God for three things before you ask for anything.", "How does your mood change when you start with thanks?"),
        PlanDay("Cause Me to Hear", "Psalms", 143, 8, 10, "Teach Me to Do Thy Will", "Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk. This is a prayer you can pray every morning. You do not know what today will bring, but you can ask the One who does to show you the way and teach you to do His will.", "Pray this psalm slowly over the day ahead of you.", "What decision today do you need God's guidance for?"),
        PlanDay("Satisfy Us Early", "Psalms", 90, 12, 17, "Establish the Work of Our Hands", "Moses asks God to satisfy us early with His mercy, so that we may rejoice all our days. He also asks God to establish the work of our hands. Morning prayer is not an escape from the day's work. It is asking God to make that work count. Whatever you do today, it can be offered to Him.", "Ask God to bless the work of your hands today.", "What work will you offer to God today?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_7 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "money-and-provision",
    title = "Money and Provision",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Seven days on trusting God with money, whether you have too little or are learning what to do with more.",
    verse = "But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.",
    verseRef = "Philippians 4:19",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_2,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("The Barrel of Meal", "1 Kings", 17, 8, 16, "Make Me Thereof a Little Cake First", "The widow of Zarephath had a handful of flour and a little oil. She was preparing a last meal for herself and her son. Elijah asked her to feed him first and trust God for the rest. She did, and the meal did not run out. God often meets our need in daily portions, enough for today, and then enough again tomorrow.", "Tell God exactly what you need this month.", "Where do you need to trust God for daily provision?"),
        PlanDay("Neither Poverty nor Riches", "Proverbs", 30, 7, 9, "Food Convenient for Me", "Agur prays a careful prayer: give me neither poverty nor riches. He knows that too little can tempt us to steal, and too much can tempt us to forget God. Few people pray for enough. Most of us pray for more. This prayer asks for what we need and for a heart that stays close to God either way.", "Ask God for enough, and for a heart that does not forget Him.", "Would your faith be stronger with more money, or weaker?"),
        PlanDay("Power to Get Wealth", "Deuteronomy", 8, 11, 18, "Remember the LORD", "When Israel was about to enter a good land, God warned them not to say, My power and the might of mine hand hath gotten me this wealth. Every good thing we earn comes through the strength He gives. Hard work matters, but so does humility. Remembering that God is the source keeps money from becoming our master.", "Thank God for every income and skill you have.", "Do you think of your money as yours or as God's?"),
        PlanDay("Godliness with Contentment", "1 Timothy", 6, 6, 12, "We Brought Nothing", "godliness with contentment is great gain. We brought nothing into this world and can carry nothing out. Paul warns that the love of money, not money itself, is a root of all kinds of evil. The pressure to have more is everywhere. Contentment is not giving up on a better life. It is refusing to let money decide whether life is good.", "Ask God to teach you contentment where you are.", "What do you find yourself wanting that you do not need?"),
        PlanDay("Prove Me Now", "Malachi", 3, 8, 12, "The Windows of Heaven", "God told Israel that by holding back their offerings they had robbed Him. Then He invited them to test Him. Giving is an act of trust. It says God, not my savings, is my security. Whatever your church teaches about tithing, the heart of this passage is clear: we honour God first with what we have, and He is faithful.", "Ask God how He wants you to give, and to make you faithful in it.", "What would giving first, rather than last, look like for you?"),
        PlanDay("Rich Toward God", "Luke", 12, 13, 21, "Thou Fool", "The rich man in Jesus' story had a good harvest and planned bigger barns. His mistake was not his success. It was that he planned his whole life around himself and never thought of God or his neighbour. That night his soul was required of him. Jesus asks us to be rich toward God: generous, grateful and ready.", "Ask God to show you one way to be rich toward Him this week.", "What are you storing up, and for whom?"),
        PlanDay("A Cheerful Giver", "2 Corinthians", 9, 6, 11, "God Loveth a Cheerful Giver", "Paul says, Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity. God does not want guilty giving or pressured giving. He loves a cheerful giver. And He is able to make all grace abound toward you, so that you have enough and something left over for every good work.", "Ask God to make you a cheerful giver.", "Who could you bless with what you have this week?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_8 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "work-and-calling",
    title = "Work and Calling",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Seven days on doing your daily work for God, whatever that work is.",
    verse = "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.",
    verseRef = "Proverbs 16:3",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_1,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("To Dress It and to Keep It", "Genesis", 2, 8, 15, "Work Before the Fall", "Before sin entered the world, God put Adam in the garden to dress it and to keep it. Work is not a punishment. It was part of the good life God designed from the start. Sin has made work harder and often frustrating, but work itself is still a way to care for God's world and serve the people in it.", "Thank God for your work, even the parts you find hard.", "How might your work be part of caring for God's world?"),
        PlanDay("As to the Lord", "Colossians", 3, 17, 25, "Not unto Men", "Paul was writing to servants with little power over their working lives. He told them to work heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men. Your boss may not notice. Your customers may not thank you. But whatever you do, you do it for Christ, and He sees all of it. That changes how we work on an ordinary Tuesday.", "Ask God to help you work today as if He were your employer.", "Who are you really working for?"),
        PlanDay("Filled with Wisdom", "Exodus", 31, 1, 6, "Bezaleel", "The first person in Scripture said to be filled with the Spirit of God was not a priest but a craftsman. Bezaleel was given skill to work in gold, silver, wood and stone. Your gifts at work, whether with your hands, with numbers or with people, can be gifts from God. He cares about skill and craft, not only sermons.", "Thank God for the abilities He has given you, and ask Him to grow them.", "What skill do you have that you have never thought of as a gift from God?"),
        PlanDay("Let Us Rise Up and Build", "Nehemiah", 2, 17, 20, "The God of Heaven Will Prosper Us", "Nehemiah saw the broken walls of Jerusalem and called the people to rebuild. Some mocked him. He answered, The God of heaven, he will prosper us; therefore we his servants will arise and build. Some work feels like rebuilding ruins. It is slow, and people may laugh. Begin anyway, and trust God to prosper what you build for Him.", "Ask God for courage to start the work He has put in front of you.", "What broken thing is God calling you to help rebuild?"),
        PlanDay("Go to the Ant", "Proverbs", 6, 6, 11, "Consider Her Ways", "The ant has no boss standing over her, yet she prepares her food in summer. Proverbs is practical. Laziness creeps in slowly, a little sleep, a little folding of the hands. Diligence is part of faithfulness. God provides, but He often provides through the work He gives us strength to do. Be steady and prepare.", "Ask God to help you be faithful in the small tasks of today.", "Where have you been putting off work you know you should do?"),
        PlanDay("Before I Formed Thee", "Jeremiah", 1, 4, 10, "I Am a Child", "God told Jeremiah that He knew him and set him apart before he was born. Jeremiah's answer was, I cannot speak: for I am a child. God did not argue about his abilities. He said, I am with thee. A calling is not about feeling ready. It is about the One who calls. He puts His words in our mouths and goes with us.", "Ask God to show you what He has made you for.", "Where have you been saying I cannot when God is saying I am with thee?"),
        PlanDay("Whatsoever Thy Hand Findeth", "Ecclesiastes", 9, 7, 10, "Do It with Thy Might", "The Preacher says, Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might. Life is short. We do not get to choose every task, but we can choose how we do the ones in front of us. Eat your bread with joy. Enjoy the people you love. Do your work well. These ordinary things, done for God, are not small.", "Ask God to help you find joy in your work and your daily life.", "What is in your hand to do today?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_9 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "singleness",
    title = "Singleness",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Five days for single people, on a life that is full and seen by God, married or not.",
    verse = "Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 16:11",
    art = Res.drawable.rhythm_reflection,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Pleasant Places", "Psalms", 16, 5, 11, "My Portion", "David says, The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places. He did not mean that everything had gone his way. He meant that God Himself was his portion, his share, the best part of his life. Singleness is not a waiting room before real life begins. If the Lord is your portion, your life now is already full of His presence.", "Thank God for the good things in your life as it is today.", "Do you see your life now as real life, or as waiting for it to begin?"),
        PlanDay("Without Distraction", "1 Corinthians", 7, 32, 35, "Undivided", "Paul, who was single himself, saw something good in it. The unmarried can care for the things of the Lord with an undivided heart. He does not look down on marriage, and he does not pity the single. Each has its own gifts and its own struggles. Ask God how your season can be used well for Him and for others.", "Ask God to show you how to use this season of your life for Him.", "What freedom does your season give you that you might be overlooking?"),
        PlanDay("Under Whose Wings", "Ruth", 2, 8, 12, "A Full Reward", "Ruth was a widow in a foreign land, gleaning in a field to feed herself and her mother-in-law. Boaz noticed her faithfulness and blessed her: a full reward be given thee of the LORD God of Israel, under whose wings thou art come to trust. Ruth was seen by God long before she was seen by Boaz. So are you.", "Thank God that He sees your faithfulness when no one else does.", "Where do you most need to know you are seen by God?"),
        PlanDay("The Solitary in Families", "Psalms", 68, 3, 6, "A Father to the Fatherless", "God setteth the solitary in families. He knows loneliness is real, and He does not leave the lonely without people. The church is meant to be a family where single people belong fully, not a place where they are an afterthought. Ask God to give you family in Him, and to make you family for others who are alone.", "Ask God for deep friendships and a church family where you belong.", "Who in your church could you draw closer to?"),
        PlanDay("The Desires of Thine Heart", "Psalms", 37, 3, 7, "Delight Thyself in the LORD", "Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart. This is not a trick for getting a spouse. When we delight in God, our desires are shaped by Him, and He meets them in His way and time. You can bring your longing for marriage honestly to Him. Then rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him.", "Bring your hopes about marriage to God honestly, and leave them with Him.", "What would it look like to delight in God this week, whatever your status?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_10 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "healing-and-wholeness",
    title = "Healing and Wholeness",
    topic = "Healing",
    blurb = "Seven days for the sick and those who pray for them, on the God who heals.",
    verse = "Heal me, O LORD, and I shall be healed; save me, and I shall be saved: for thou art my praise.",
    verseRef = "Jeremiah 17:14",
    art = Res.drawable.onboarding_pray_v3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Go and Wash", "2 Kings", 5, 9, 14, "Naaman", "Naaman was a great man with leprosy. He expected a dramatic healing and was angry when told simply to wash in the Jordan seven times. His servants persuaded him, and he was healed. God does not always heal in the way we expect. Sometimes the path to healing is humble and ordinary: a treatment, a habit, a plain step of obedience.", "Ask God to heal you in His way, and to help you take any humble step He shows you.", "Is there a simple step toward healing you have been resisting?"),
        PlanDay("What Wilt Thou?", "Mark", 10, 46, 52, "Blind Bartimaeus", "Bartimaeus cried out, and people told him to be quiet. He cried all the more. Jesus stopped and asked him, What wilt thou that I should do unto thee? Jesus already knew, but He wanted to hear it. You are allowed to ask God plainly for healing. Do not let anyone quiet your cry. He stops for those who call.", "Tell Jesus plainly what you want Him to do for you.", "If Jesus asked you that question today, what would you say?"),
        PlanDay("That the Works of God", "John", 9, 1, 7, "Who Did Sin?", "The disciples assumed the blind man's condition was someone's fault. Jesus said no. Sickness is not always a punishment. Many people carry shame along with their illness, as if they must have done something wrong. Jesus lifts that weight. He says this is a place where the works of God should be made manifest. God is at work here too.", "Ask God to lift any shame you carry about your sickness.", "Have you believed that your illness is a punishment?"),
        PlanDay("For I Am Weak", "Psalms", 6, 1, 9, "My Bones Are Vexed", "David prays from his sickbed: have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I am weak. He is honest about being exhausted, about tears that soak his bed. Then he says, the LORD hath heard the voice of my weeping. You do not need strong words when you are sick. Weeping is a voice God hears.", "Pray honestly about how weak and tired you feel.", "What would you say to God if you did not have to sound strong?"),
        PlanDay("Such as I Have", "Acts", 3, 1, 8, "Walking and Leaping", "A man lame from birth asked Peter and John for money. Peter said, Silver and gold have I none; but such as I have give I thee. Then he raised him up in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth. The man went into the temple walking, leaping and praising God. Jesus still heals, and still uses ordinary people praying in His name.", "Pray in Jesus' name for someone you know who is sick.", "Who could you pray for in person this week?"),
        PlanDay("I Have Seen Thy Tears", "2 Kings", 20, 1, 6, "Hezekiah's Prayer", "Hezekiah was told he would die. He turned his face to the wall and prayed and wept. Before Isaiah had left the courtyard, God sent him back: I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears. God gave Hezekiah fifteen more years. Not every prayer for healing is answered this way, but every one is heard, and every tear is seen.", "Pour out your heart to God about your health, holding nothing back.", "What do you want to say to God that you have not yet said?"),
        PlanDay("The Healing of the Nations", "Revelation", 22, 1, 5, "No More Curse", "At the end of the Bible there is a river of life and a tree whose leaves are for the healing of the nations. there shall be no more curse. Some healing comes in this life. Complete healing comes when Christ makes all things new. Whether you are healed today or still waiting, this is where your story is going, and it is good.", "Thank God for the day when there will be no more sickness or pain.", "How does the promise of final healing help you today?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_11 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "overcoming-fear",
    title = "Overcoming Fear",
    topic = "Peace",
    blurb = "Seven days of courage from Scripture for the fears that hold you back.",
    verse = "Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.",
    verseRef = "Isaiah 41:10",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_5,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Be Strong and of a Good Courage", "Joshua", 1, 5, 9, "Whithersoever Thou Goest", "Joshua had to lead a nation after Moses died. God told him three times to be strong and courageous. Courage is not the absence of fear. If Joshua had not been afraid, God would not have needed to say it so often. The reason for courage is not in Joshua at all. It is this: the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.", "Ask God for courage for the thing you are most afraid of.", "What is God asking you to do even though you are afraid?"),
        PlanDay("The LORD Is on My Side", "Psalms", 118, 5, 9, "What Can Man Do?", "The LORD is on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me? Much of our fear is fear of people: what they think, what they might do, whether they will reject us. The psalmist learned that it is better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in man. When He is on your side, people lose their power to rule you.", "Ask God to free you from the fear of what people think.", "Whose opinion do you fear most?"),
        PlanDay("Whom Shall I Fear?", "Psalms", 27, 1, 5, "My Light and My Salvation", "The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? David faced real enemies and real armies. He did not pretend they were not there. He set beside them a bigger truth: God was his light, his salvation, his strength. Fear shrinks when it is held next to who God is. Say this verse aloud today, slowly, and mean it.", "Speak Psalm 27:1 aloud over your situation.", "What would change if you really believed God was your strength?"),
        PlanDay("Be Not Afraid, Only Believe", "Mark", 5, 35, 43, "Talitha Cumi", "Jairus had just been told his daughter was dead. Jesus heard and said to him, Be not afraid, only believe. When the worst news comes, fear rushes in. Jesus speaks into that moment. He took Jairus with Him to the house, past the mourners, to the child's bed, and raised her up. He does not leave us alone with bad news.", "Ask Jesus to speak His word into the worst news you have received.", "What news has filled you with fear?"),
        PlanDay("Not the Spirit of Fear", "2 Timothy", 1, 6, 10, "Power, Love and a Sound Mind", "Timothy seems to have been timid. Paul reminds him, God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind. Fear is not from God. What He gives is power to act, love for others and a steady, clear mind. Stir up the gift in you. You do not have to live ruled by fear.", "Ask God to fill you with power, love and a sound mind.", "Where has fear been making your decisions?"),
        PlanDay("Perfect Love Casteth Out Fear", "1 John", 4, 15, 19, "We Love Him", "There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear. Some of our deepest fears are about God Himself: that He will reject us or punish us. John says that fear does not belong in the life of someone who knows God's love. The more you understand how much He loves you, the less room fear has.", "Ask God to show you how much He loves you.", "Are you afraid of God in a way that keeps you from Him?"),
        PlanDay("When Thou Passest Through the Waters", "Isaiah", 43, 1, 3, "Thou Art Mine", "God does not promise that you will never pass through deep waters or fire. He promises, When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee. And before that, He says, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine. You belong to Him. Whatever you pass through, you will not go through it alone.", "Thank God that you are His, and that He goes through the waters with you.", "What waters are you passing through right now?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_12 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "hearing-gods-voice",
    title = "Hearing God's Voice",
    topic = "Prayer",
    blurb = "Seven days on how God speaks, and how to listen.",
    verse = "And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.",
    verseRef = "Isaiah 30:21",
    art = Res.drawable.onboarding_audio_v3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("They Know His Voice", "John", 10, 1, 6, "The Shepherd Calls by Name", "Jesus says the shepherd calls his own sheep by name and leads them out, and they follow because they know his voice. Sheep learn their shepherd's voice by spending time with him. Hearing God is not a special skill for a few. It grows as we spend time with Him in His word and in prayer, day after ordinary day.", "Ask Jesus to help you know His voice.", "How much time do you spend listening to God compared with talking?"),
        PlanDay("A Still Small Voice", "1 Kings", 19, 9, 13, "Not in the Wind", "Elijah was worn out and afraid. God passed by, and there was a great wind, an earthquake and a fire, but the Lord was not in them. After the fire came a still small voice. We often look for God in the dramatic. He often speaks quietly. To hear Him, we may need to switch off some of the noise.", "Spend five minutes in quiet before God today, without music or your phone.", "What noise in your life might be drowning out God's voice?"),
        PlanDay("A Lamp unto My Feet", "Psalms", 119, 105, 112, "Thy Word", "Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path. The main way God speaks is through Scripture. A lamp in those days lit only a few steps ahead, not the whole road. God's word may not show you the next ten years. It will show you the next step. Anything that claims to be from God will agree with His word.", "Ask God to speak to you as you read the Bible this week.", "When has a verse spoken directly to your situation?"),
        PlanDay("This Is the Way", "Isaiah", 30, 18, 21, "A Word Behind Thee", "God promises His people, thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it. Notice that this comes after a promise of grace and of an answered cry. God is not hiding His will from you. He is more willing to guide you than you are to be guided. Trust Him to correct you if you turn aside.", "Ask God to guide you in a decision you are facing.", "Where do you need God to say, this is the way?"),
        PlanDay("He Will Guide You", "John", 16, 12, 15, "The Spirit of Truth", "Jesus told His disciples there was more He wanted to say, but they could not bear it yet. The Spirit of truth would come and guide them into all truth. The Holy Spirit does not speak on His own; He takes what is Christ's and shows it to us. What the Spirit says will always look like Jesus.", "Ask the Holy Spirit to guide you into truth.", "Does what you think God is saying look like Jesus?"),
        PlanDay("To Day If Ye Will Hear", "Hebrews", 3, 7, 15, "Harden Not Your Hearts", "To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts. Hearing God is not only about listening; it is about being willing to obey. A heart can grow hard slowly, by ignoring what God has already said. If you want to hear more, begin by responding to what you have already heard. Today is the day to answer.", "Ask God to soften your heart toward anything He has already told you.", "What has God already said that you have not yet obeyed?"),
        PlanDay("Doers of the Word", "James", 1, 19, 25, "Swift to Hear", "James says, be swift to hear, slow to speak. Then he warns against hearing without doing. Someone who hears God's word and ignores it is like a man who looks in a mirror and forgets his own face. Listening to God changes us only when we act on what we hear. Pick one thing He has shown you this week and do it.", "Ask God for the courage to act on what He says.", "What is one thing God has shown you that you will do today?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_13 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "the-lords-prayer",
    title = "The Lord's Prayer",
    topic = "Prayer",
    blurb = "Seven days through the prayer Jesus taught, one line at a time.",
    verse = "After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.",
    verseRef = "Matthew 6:9",
    art = Res.drawable.prayerkey_hero_dawn,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("The Prayer Jesus Taught", "Matthew", 6, 9, 13, "After This Manner", "Jesus said, After this manner therefore pray ye. He gave a pattern, not just words to repeat. It begins with God and His glory, then turns to our needs: bread, forgiveness and protection. Then it ends where it began, with God: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever. This week, we take it one line at a time.", "Pray the Lord's Prayer slowly, pausing after each line.", "Which line of this prayer means the most to you?"),
        PlanDay("Our Father", "1 John", 3, 1, 3, "What Manner of Love", "The prayer begins with two words that change everything: Our Father. Not my Father only, but ours. You pray as part of a family. And He is Father, not a distant power. Behold, what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called the sons of God. You come to Him as a child, welcome.", "Come to God today as a child to a loving Father.", "How does it feel to call God Father?"),
        PlanDay("Hallowed Be Thy Name", "Isaiah", 6, 1, 5, "Holy, Holy, Holy", "Isaiah saw the Lord high and lifted up, and the seraphims cried, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts. To hallow God's name is to treat Him as holy, to honour Him above everything. Prayer is not only bringing our list. It begins with worship, with remembering who we are speaking to. That puts our needs in their right place.", "Spend the first part of your prayer today only praising God.", "What helps you remember how holy God is?"),
        PlanDay("Thy Will Be Done", "Luke", 22, 39, 46, "Not My Will", "In the garden, Jesus prayed, not my will, but thine, be done. It was the hardest prayer of His life. Thy kingdom come, thy will be done is not a passive prayer. It asks God to bring His rule into our world and into our own hearts, even when His will is not what we would choose. Jesus prayed it first.", "Surrender one situation to God's will today.", "Where do you find it hardest to pray thy will be done?"),
        PlanDay("Our Daily Bread", "Exodus", 16, 14, 18, "Manna", "In the wilderness, God sent manna every morning. Each person gathered what they needed for that day, no more. he that gathered much had nothing over, and he that gathered little had no lack. Give us this day our daily bread is a prayer of trust for today. Tomorrow's bread will come tomorrow. God is not running out.", "Ask God for what you need today, and trust Him for tomorrow.", "What do you need from God today?"),
        PlanDay("Forgive Us Our Debts", "Matthew", 6, 12, 15, "As We Forgive", "This is the only line Jesus explained after the prayer. if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you. Being forgiven and forgiving others are tied together. We cannot hold tightly to God's mercy with one hand while holding a grudge with the other. Ask Him to forgive you, and to help you forgive.", "Ask God's forgiveness, and name before Him someone you need to forgive.", "Who do you need to forgive as you pray this line?"),
        PlanDay("Deliver Us from Evil", "1 Corinthians", 10, 11, 14, "A Way to Escape", "Lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. We pray this because we know we are weak. Paul gives a promise: God is faithful, and with every temptation He will make a way to escape. The prayer then closes in praise. The kingdom, the power and the glory are His. We end our prayers sure of who is in charge.", "Ask God to show you the way of escape from a temptation you face.", "What temptation do you most need God to deliver you from?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_14 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "psalms-of-comfort",
    title = "The Psalms of Comfort",
    topic = "Peace",
    blurb = "Ten psalms for hard days, to read slowly and pray as your own.",
    verse = "God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 46:1",
    art = Res.drawable.verse_card_botanical,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("The LORD Is My Shepherd", "Psalms", 23, 1, 6, "I Shall Not Want", "This may be the best-known passage in the Bible, and for good reason. The shepherd leads, restores, walks with us through the valley of the shadow of death, and prepares a table even in front of enemies. Read it slowly today, as if for the first time. Put your own name in it. He is your shepherd.", "Pray Psalm 23 aloud, slowly, as your own prayer.", "Which line of Psalm 23 do you need most today?"),
        PlanDay("A Very Present Help", "Psalms", 46, 1, 11, "Be Still", "The earth shakes, the mountains fall into the sea, nations rage. And in the middle of it all: Be still, and know that I am God. This psalm does not promise that the ground will never shake. It promises that God is a refuge and strength, present right now, in the trouble, not far from it.", "Sit quietly for a few minutes and rest in the fact that God is God.", "What is shaking in your life right now?"),
        PlanDay("My Strength", "Psalms", 18, 1, 6, "I Will Love Thee, O LORD", "David wrote this after God delivered him from Saul. He piles up names for God: rock, fortress, deliverer, buckler, high tower. When he was surrounded by sorrows, he called, and God heard him from His temple. Try naming God today by what He has been to you. It is one way to remember that He has not changed.", "Thank God by name for what He has been to you.", "What name for God fits what you need right now?"),
        PlanDay("He Shall Give His Angels Charge", "Psalms", 91, 9, 16, "I Will Be with Him", "The psalm ends with God speaking: He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I will be with him in trouble. The promise is not that trouble will never come, but that He will be with you in it, and will deliver. You have made the Lord your refuge. He takes that seriously.", "Call on God today and thank Him that He answers.", "When has God been with you in trouble?"),
        PlanDay("Thou Hast Searched Me", "Psalms", 139, 1, 12, "Whither Shall I Go?", "There is nowhere you can go that God is not already there. Not the heights or the depths, not the far side of the sea, not the darkest night. the darkness and the light are both alike to thee. You are fully known and still loved. That is a great comfort for anyone who feels lost or alone.", "Thank God that He knows you completely and loves you still.", "Where have you felt far from God?"),
        PlanDay("My Soul Waiteth upon God", "Psalms", 62, 1, 8, "Pour Out Your Heart", "David tells his soul to wait only upon God. Then he turns to us: pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. You do not have to tidy up your feelings before you pray. Pour them out, all of them. God is strong enough to hold them and kind enough to listen.", "Pour out your heart to God today, with no editing.", "What have you been holding back from God?"),
        PlanDay("In the Day of My Trouble", "Psalms", 86, 1, 7, "Bow Down Thine Ear", "Bow down thine ear, O LORD, hear me: for I am poor and needy. David is not embarrassed to say he is in need. Then he says, In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee: for thou wilt answer me. He speaks with confidence, not because his troubles are small, but because his God is good and ready to forgive.", "Tell God plainly where you are poor and needy.", "What trouble do you need to bring to God today?"),
        PlanDay("Return unto Thy Rest", "Psalms", 116, 1, 9, "He Hath Heard My Voice", "The psalmist was close to death, full of trouble and sorrow. He called on the Lord and was delivered. Now he says, Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee. Sometimes we need to speak to our own souls and remind them where rest is found.", "Tell your soul today to return to its rest in God.", "What would it mean for your soul to rest?"),
        PlanDay("As a Weaned Child", "Psalms", 131, 1, 3, "Quieted", "This is one of the shortest psalms. David says he has stopped trying to handle things too great for him. He has quieted himself as a child that is weaned of his mother. A weaned child sits with its mother not because it wants something, but simply to be near her. Can you sit with God like that today?", "Sit with God today without asking for anything.", "What are you trying to carry that is too great for you?"),
        PlanDay("The LORD Upholdeth All That Fall", "Psalms", 145, 13, 21, "Nigh unto All That Call", "The LORD upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all those that be bowed down. If you are bowed down today, this is for you. He is near to all who call on Him in truth. He hears their cry and saves them. Read the psalm through again, and let it lift your head.", "Ask God to raise you up where you are bowed down.", "Which of these ten psalms will you return to?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_15 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "sermon-on-the-mount",
    title = "The Sermon on the Mount",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Ten days through Jesus' best-known teaching, Matthew 5 to 7.",
    verse = "Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.",
    verseRef = "Matthew 5:16",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Blessed Are the Poor in Spirit", "Matthew", 5, 1, 12, "The Beatitudes", "Jesus begins by calling blessed the people the world overlooks: the poor in spirit, the mourners, the meek, the hungry for righteousness. His kingdom turns things upside down. You do not need to have it all together to be blessed by God. Often it is when you know your need most that you are closest to His kingdom.", "Ask God to make you poor in spirit and hungry for righteousness.", "Which of these blessings do you most need to hear today?"),
        PlanDay("Salt and Light", "Matthew", 5, 13, 16, "Let Your Light So Shine", "Jesus did not say, try to become salt and light. He said, ye are. Salt preserves and flavours; light shows the way. A follower of Jesus is meant to make a difference simply by living as one. Do not hide it. Let people see your good works, so that they glorify your Father, not you.", "Ask God for one way to be salt and light today.", "Where is God placing you to shine?"),
        PlanDay("First Be Reconciled", "Matthew", 5, 21, 26, "Anger", "Jesus goes beyond the act of murder to the anger that starts it. He says that if you are bringing your gift to the altar and remember someone has something against you, leave your gift and first be reconciled to thy brother. God cares about our relationships as much as our worship. Peace with others is part of peace with Him.", "Ask God to show you any relationship you need to make right.", "Is there someone you need to be reconciled to?"),
        PlanDay("Love Your Enemies", "Matthew", 5, 38, 48, "Children of Your Father", "Love your enemies, bless them that curse you. This is one of the hardest things Jesus ever said. He grounds it in the Father, who sends rain on the just and the unjust. Loving an enemy does not mean letting them harm you. It means wishing them good, praying for them and refusing to become like them.", "Pray today for someone who has wronged you.", "Who is the hardest person for you to bless?"),
        PlanDay("In Secret", "Matthew", 6, 1, 4, "Thy Father Which Seeth", "Jesus warns against doing good to be seen by people. If that is the goal, being seen is the only reward. Give in secret, and your Father who sees in secret will reward you. There is a quiet joy in doing good that no one knows about except God. It keeps the heart honest.", "Do one good thing today that no one will know about.", "Why do you do the good things you do?"),
        PlanDay("Treasure in Heaven", "Matthew", 6, 19, 24, "Where Your Heart Is", "where your treasure is, there will your heart be also. Our hearts follow our treasure. Jesus says plainly that we cannot serve God and money. Earthly things wear out, rust or get stolen. What we give to God and to people in His name is never lost. Look at where your money and time go, and you will see where your heart is.", "Ask God to set your heart on what lasts.", "What does your spending say about your heart?"),
        PlanDay("Take No Thought", "Matthew", 6, 25, 34, "Consider the Lilies", "Jesus points to the birds and the flowers. They do not worry, and your heavenly Father feeds and clothes them. You are worth much more. Worry adds nothing to your life. Instead, seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you. Live today, and trust Him for tomorrow.", "Hand God one worry about tomorrow.", "What would seeking first the kingdom look like today?"),
        PlanDay("Judge Not", "Matthew", 7, 1, 5, "The Beam in Thine Own Eye", "It is easy to see the speck in someone else's eye and miss the beam in our own. Jesus does not say never discern right from wrong. He says, deal with yourself first. Humility makes us gentle with others. When we know how much we have been forgiven, we stop measuring people with a harsh rule.", "Ask God to show you the beam in your own eye.", "Whom have you been judging harshly?"),
        PlanDay("Ask, Seek, Knock", "Matthew", 7, 7, 12, "Good Things", "Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you. Jesus invites persistent prayer. Then He reasons from earthly parents: if you, being evil, give good gifts to your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him? Keep asking.", "Bring to God again something you have stopped asking for.", "What have you given up asking God for?"),
        PlanDay("The Wise Man Built upon a Rock", "Matthew", 7, 24, 29, "Hear and Do", "Both houses faced the same storm. The difference was the foundation. The wise man hears Jesus' words and does them. The foolish man hears and does not. After ten days in this sermon, the question is not how much we have heard but what we will do. Build on the rock, and you will stand.", "Ask God to help you put one teaching from this sermon into practice.", "Which teaching from these ten days will you act on?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_16 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "life-of-jesus",
    title = "The Life of Jesus",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Fourteen days through the life of Jesus, from the angel's visit to Mary to the day He was taken up.",
    verse = "And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.",
    verseRef = "John 1:14",
    art = Res.drawable.onboarding_read_v3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("The Angel Comes to Mary", "Luke", 1, 26, 38, "Be It unto Me", "God chose a young woman from a small town to carry His Son. Mary was troubled and asked how it could be. The angel answered, with God nothing shall be impossible. Mary's reply is one of the most beautiful in Scripture: be it unto me according to thy word. The story of Jesus begins with a yes.", "Say yes to God today in whatever He is asking of you.", "What is God asking you to say yes to?"),
        PlanDay("Born in Bethlehem", "Luke", 2, 4, 14, "No Room in the Inn", "The Son of God was born where animals were fed, because there was no room for them in the inn. The first to hear were shepherds working the night shift. Jesus came low, to ordinary people, without power or money. No one is too poor or too plain to be welcome at His manger. The good tidings are for all people.", "Thank God that Jesus came to ordinary people like you.", "Is there room for Jesus in your life right now?"),
        PlanDay("In My Father's House", "Luke", 2, 41, 52, "The Boy in the Temple", "At twelve, Jesus stayed behind in Jerusalem, listening to the teachers and asking questions. When His worried parents found Him, He said, wist ye not that I must be about my Father's business? Then He went home and was subject to them. Even as a boy, He knew who His Father was, and He grew in wisdom and stature.", "Ask God to help you grow in wisdom and in favour with Him.", "What does being about your Father's business look like for you?"),
        PlanDay("This Is My Beloved Son", "Matthew", 3, 13, 17, "The Baptism", "Before Jesus preached one sermon or did one miracle, the Father spoke from heaven: This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. The Father's love came first, before the work. In Christ, the same is true for you. You are loved before you achieve anything. Ministry and work flow from that love; they do not earn it.", "Thank God that you are loved before you do anything for Him.", "Do you live as someone already loved, or as someone trying to earn it?"),
        PlanDay("The Wedding at Cana", "John", 2, 1, 11, "Whatsoever He Saith", "Jesus' first sign was at a village wedding when the wine ran out. It saved a family from shame. Mary told the servants, Whatsoever he saith unto you, do it. They filled jars with water, and it became the best wine. Jesus cares about the ordinary troubles of ordinary people. He is still the one to bring them to.", "Bring Jesus a small, practical need in your life today.", "What has run out in your life that you need Jesus to fill?"),
        PlanDay("Follow Me", "Mark", 1, 14, 20, "Fishers of Men", "Jesus walked by the sea and called fishermen at work: Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men. They left their nets straightway. Jesus does not wait for people to be ready. He calls them in the middle of ordinary life and promises to make them into something new. He still calls today.", "Ask Jesus what following Him means for you this week.", "What nets might Jesus be asking you to leave?"),
        PlanDay("Thy Sins Be Forgiven", "Mark", 2, 1, 12, "Four Friends and a Roof", "Four men could not get their paralysed friend to Jesus through the crowd, so they opened up the roof. Jesus saw their faith and first said, Son, thy sins be forgiven thee. Then He healed him. Jesus deals with our deepest need first. And sometimes our friends' faith carries us to Him when we cannot walk ourselves.", "Pray for a friend who needs Jesus, and ask how you might bring them to Him.", "Who are the friends who carry you to Jesus?"),
        PlanDay("Five Loaves and Two Fishes", "Mark", 6, 34, 44, "Give Ye Them to Eat", "Jesus was moved with compassion because the people were as sheep not having a shepherd. The disciples wanted to send them away. Jesus said, Give ye them to eat. Five loaves and two fishes, given to Him, fed thousands, with baskets left over. What you have may look small. Put it in His hands, and see what He does.", "Offer God whatever small thing you have, and ask Him to use it.", "What do you have that seems too small to matter?"),
        PlanDay("Zacchaeus", "Luke", 19, 1, 10, "To Day I Must Abide at Thy House", "Zacchaeus was rich, small and disliked. He climbed a tree to see Jesus. Jesus stopped, looked up and called him by name: make haste, and come down; for to day I must abide at thy house. The crowd murmured. Jesus did not care. the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost. Nobody is too far gone.", "Thank Jesus that He came looking for you.", "Who do you think is too far from God?"),
        PlanDay("The Transfiguration", "Matthew", 17, 1, 8, "Jesus Only", "On the mountain, Jesus' face shone like the sun, and Moses and Elijah appeared. Peter, not knowing what to say, offered to build shelters. Then the cloud came, and the Father said, hear ye him. When the disciples looked up, they saw no man, save Jesus only. In the end, it all comes down to Him.", "Ask God to help you listen to Jesus above every other voice.", "What would it mean to see Jesus only in your situation?"),
        PlanDay("He Washed Their Feet", "John", 13, 1, 15, "I Have Given You an Example", "Knowing that the Father had given all things into His hands, Jesus took a towel and washed His disciples' feet. It was a servant's job. Peter objected. Jesus said this was what love looks like. I have given you an example. The greatest in His kingdom are the ones who kneel and serve.", "Ask God to show you someone to serve humbly today.", "Whose feet is Jesus asking you to wash?"),
        PlanDay("It Is Finished", "John", 19, 25, 30, "At the Cross", "Even on the cross, Jesus cared for His mother, giving her into John's keeping. Then He said, It is finished, bowed His head and gave up the ghost. The work of salvation was complete. Nothing remains to be added. You cannot add to it, and you do not have to. Stand at the cross today and simply thank Him.", "Thank Jesus for what He finished on the cross for you.", "What are you still trying to add to what Jesus finished?"),
        PlanDay("He Is Risen", "Luke", 24, 1, 12, "Why Seek Ye the Living?", "The women came early with spices for a dead body. The stone was rolled away. Two men in shining garments asked, Why seek ye the living among the dead? He is not here, but is risen. The disciples thought it was idle tales. It was the truest news the world has ever heard. Jesus is alive.", "Thank God that Jesus is alive today.", "What difference does the resurrection make to your life this week?"),
        PlanDay("Taken Up", "Acts", 1, 6, 11, "Ye Shall Be Witnesses", "Before He was taken up, Jesus promised power when the Holy Ghost came, and gave His followers a task: to be His witnesses to the ends of the earth. Then the angels said He would come again in like manner. His story continues through His people. Your part in it begins today, right where you are.", "Ask God to make you a faithful witness for Jesus.", "Who is one person you could tell about Jesus?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_17 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "prayer-and-fasting",
    title = "Prayer and Fasting",
    topic = "Prayer",
    blurb = "Seven days on why God's people have fasted, and how to begin wisely.",
    verse = "And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.",
    verseRef = "Joel 2:13",
    art = Res.drawable.today_prayer_violet,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("When Ye Fast", "Matthew", 6, 16, 18, "Not to Be Seen", "Jesus said when you fast, not if. He assumed His followers would. But He warned against making a show of it. Fasting is between you and your Father, who sees in secret. A fast can be from food, or one meal, or something else that fills your time. Start small and wisely. If you have a health condition, talk to your doctor first.", "Ask God what kind of fast He is inviting you to this week, if any.", "Why would you fast, and who would you be doing it for?"),
        PlanDay("The Fast That I Have Chosen", "Isaiah", 58, 6, 11, "Loose the Bands", "Israel fasted but kept mistreating people. God said the fast He wants includes loosing the bands of wickedness, sharing bread with the hungry and bringing the poor into your house. Fasting that pleases God changes how we treat others. Then His promise comes: Then shall thy light break forth as the morning.", "Ask God to show you someone to help as part of your fast.", "How could your fasting bless someone in need?"),
        PlanDay("Rend Your Heart", "Joel", 2, 12, 17, "Turn Ye Even to Me", "rend your heart, and not your garments. In Israel, people tore their clothes to show grief. God wants more than outward signs. He wants hearts that turn back to Him. Fasting is a way of saying, I want You more than food. And God is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, ready to receive those who return.", "Ask God to turn your heart fully back to Him.", "What part of your heart has drifted from God?"),
        PlanDay("Fast Ye for Me", "Esther", 4, 13, 17, "If I Perish, I Perish", "Esther had to go before the king uninvited, which could mean death. She asked her people to fast for her three days. Then she said, if I perish, I perish. Fasting together for a need is an old practice among God's people. It joins hearts in one cry. Is there something your family or church should seek God for together?", "Pray for someone facing a hard situation, and consider fasting with them.", "Who could you fast and pray alongside?"),
        PlanDay("Seeking by Prayer and Supplications", "Daniel", 9, 3, 9, "We Have Sinned", "Daniel set his face to seek God by prayer and supplications, with fasting. His prayer was full of confession, not for himself only, but for his people. To the Lord our God belong mercies and forgivenesses. Fasting often leads to honesty before God. As the noise of appetite goes quiet, we see ourselves more clearly.", "Confess to God where you, your family or your nation have turned from Him.", "What has fasting, or quiet, shown you about yourself?"),
        PlanDay("As They Ministered and Fasted", "Acts", 13, 1, 3, "Separate Me Barnabas and Saul", "The church at Antioch was worshipping and fasting when the Holy Ghost spoke and sent out Barnabas and Saul. Then they fasted and prayed again before laying hands on them. Fasting helped them hear God's direction. If you are facing a big decision, setting aside time to pray and fast can help you listen.", "Bring a decision you are facing to God in prayer and fasting.", "What do you need direction from God about?"),
        PlanDay("Nehemiah Wept", "Nehemiah", 1, 4, 11, "Prosper Thy Servant", "When Nehemiah heard that Jerusalem's walls were broken, he sat down and wept, and mourned certain days, and fasted, and prayed. His fast led to a plan, and his plan to action. Fasting is not an escape from the world's needs. It prepares us to step into them with God. Ask Him what He wants you to build.", "Ask God to turn your prayer into action.", "What broken thing has God put on your heart?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_18 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "women-of-faith",
    title = "Women of Faith",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Seven days with women in the Bible who trusted God, and what they teach us.",
    verse = "Favour is deceitful, and beauty is vain: but a woman that feareth the LORD, she shall be praised.",
    verseRef = "Proverbs 31:30",
    art = Res.drawable.onboarding_journal_v3,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Ruth", "Ruth", 1, 14, 18, "Whither Thou Goest", "Ruth could have gone home after her husband died. Instead she told Naomi, whither thou goest, I will go, and thy God my God. She chose loyalty, a foreign land and the God of Israel. Her quiet faithfulness placed her in the family line of Jesus. God sees faithfulness that the world calls small.", "Ask God to make you faithful to the people He has given you.", "Who is God calling you to stand by?"),
        PlanDay("Hannah", "1 Samuel", 2, 1, 5, "My Heart Rejoiceth", "Hannah had been mocked for years because she had no child. She poured out her soul to God, and He answered. Her song begins, My heart rejoiceth in the LORD. She praises a God who lifts the low and humbles the proud. Hannah teaches us to pray honestly in sorrow, and to remember to give thanks when the answer comes.", "Thank God for an answered prayer you may have forgotten.", "What has God done that you need to sing about?"),
        PlanDay("Deborah", "Judges", 4, 4, 9, "I Will Surely Go with Thee", "Deborah was a prophetess and judge in Israel. When Barak would not go to battle without her, she said, I will surely go with thee. Her courage strengthened others. God has always used women to lead, counsel and stand firm. Courage in one person can make others brave too.", "Ask God to make you a source of courage for others.", "Who needs you to stand alongside them right now?"),
        PlanDay("Esther", "Esther", 4, 13, 16, "For Such a Time as This", "Mordecai told Esther, who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this? Esther was in the palace for a reason. She could have stayed silent and safe. She chose to risk her life for her people. Where you are is not an accident. God may have placed you there for someone else's sake.", "Ask God why He has placed you where you are.", "Who might you be in your position to help?"),
        PlanDay("Mary", "Luke", 1, 46, 55, "My Soul Doth Magnify the Lord", "Mary was young, poor and facing gossip. Yet her song is full of joy: My soul doth magnify the Lord. She sees God filling the hungry and lifting the lowly. Mary did not know what her yes would cost her. But she knew who God was, and that was enough to sing about.", "Praise God for who He is, apart from your circumstances.", "What does Mary's song teach you about God?"),
        PlanDay("Mary and Martha", "Luke", 10, 38, 42, "That Good Part", "Martha was busy serving and upset that her sister sat at Jesus' feet. Jesus spoke gently: Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things. Serving is good. But Mary had chosen the good part, being with Him. Many women carry heavy loads at home and at work. Jesus invites you to sit with Him too.", "Set aside time today simply to sit with Jesus.", "What are you careful and troubled about?"),
        PlanDay("Mary Magdalene", "John", 20, 11, 18, "She Turned Herself", "Mary Magdalene stayed at the empty tomb weeping when others had gone home. Jesus came and spoke one word, her name, and she knew Him. She became the first to tell the news, that she had seen the Lord. Jesus chose a woman, once troubled and now devoted, to carry the greatest message ever told.", "Thank Jesus that He knows your name.", "How would you tell someone what Jesus has done for you?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_19 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "men-of-courage",
    title = "Men of Courage",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Seven days with men in the Bible who stood firm, and what real strength looks like.",
    verse = "Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, quit you like men, be strong.",
    verseRef = "1 Corinthians 16:13",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_6,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Joseph Fled", "Genesis", 39, 7, 12, "How Can I Do This Great Wickedness?", "Joseph was young, far from home and tempted day after day. His answer was clear: how then can I do this great wickedness, and sin against God? When she grabbed him, he ran. Courage sometimes means running away. Strength is not proving you can resist temptation. It is getting out of its reach.", "Ask God for strength to flee the temptations you face.", "What temptation do you need to run from?"),
        PlanDay("Gideon", "Judges", 6, 11, 16, "Thou Mighty Man of Valour", "Gideon was hiding when the angel called him thou mighty man of valour. He did not feel mighty. He said his family was poor and he was the least. God's answer was, Surely I will be with thee. God sees what He can make of you, not just what you are now. Your courage rests on His presence.", "Ask God to show you what He sees in you.", "Where do you feel like the least?"),
        PlanDay("David and Goliath", "1 Samuel", 17, 32, 37, "The LORD That Delivered Me", "Everyone was afraid of Goliath. David remembered the lion and the bear, and how God had helped him then. The LORD that delivered me out of the paw of the lion, he said, he will deliver me. Courage grows from remembering God's faithfulness in small battles. Think back. What has God already brought you through?", "Thank God for past victories, and trust Him for the giant in front of you.", "What giant are you facing?"),
        PlanDay("Nehemiah", "Nehemiah", 4, 14, 18, "Remember the Lord", "The builders were afraid of their enemies. Nehemiah said, Be not ye afraid of them: remember the Lord, and fight for your sons, your daughters, your wives and your houses. Then they worked with one hand and held a weapon with the other. A godly man protects his family and keeps building, even when there is opposition.", "Pray for protection over your family and the work God has given you.", "What does it look like to fight for your family in prayer?"),
        PlanDay("Caleb", "Joshua", 14, 6, 12, "Give Me This Mountain", "At eighty-five, Caleb asked for the hardest land in Canaan, the hill country full of giants. Forty-five years earlier he had wholly followed the LORD. He was still following. Courage is not only for the young. Faithfulness over a long life makes a man ready for great things even late in life.", "Ask God to make you wholly devoted to Him for the long run.", "What mountain is God calling you to take?"),
        PlanDay("As for Me and My House", "Joshua", 24, 14, 18, "Choose You This Day", "Joshua stood before the nation and made his choice public: as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD. He did not wait to see what others would do. A man who leads his home in faith does not need to be loud or harsh. He needs to be clear about whom he serves, and to live it.", "Make your own choice before God today to serve Him with your household.", "What does serving the Lord look like in your home?"),
        PlanDay("They Had Been with Jesus", "Acts", 4, 8, 13, "The Boldness of Peter and John", "The leaders saw the boldness of Peter and John and marvelled, because they were unlearned and ignorant men. Then they realised that they had been with Jesus. Boldness did not come from education or status. It came from time with Jesus and the filling of the Spirit. That is where true courage comes from.", "Spend time with Jesus today, and ask Him for holy boldness.", "Can people tell that you have been with Jesus?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_20 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "students-and-exams",
    title = "Students and Exams",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Five days for students, before and during exams, on study, worry and wisdom.",
    verse = "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.",
    verseRef = "James 1:5",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_4,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Knowledge and Skill", "Daniel", 1, 17, 20, "Ten Times Better", "Daniel and his friends were students in a foreign land. God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom. They also worked hard and stayed faithful to Him. God cares about your studies. Ask Him for understanding, then do your part: attend, read, revise. Faith and hard work belong together.", "Ask God for understanding as you study today.", "How could you invite God into your study time?"),
        PlanDay("Search for Her", "Proverbs", 2, 1, 6, "As for Hid Treasures", "Proverbs says wisdom is found by the one who searchest for her as for hid treasures. Treasure is not found by accident; it is dug for. Learning takes effort, and so does wisdom. But the promise is sure: the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding. Dig, and ask.", "Ask God to give you a love of learning, not just a wish to pass.", "What would it look like to study as if searching for treasure?"),
        PlanDay("Be Careful for Nothing", "Philippians", 4, 6, 8, "Exam Nerves", "Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God. Careful here means anxious. Exam nerves are normal. Bring them to God. Then think on what is true and good, not on every bad result your mind can imagine. His peace can guard your heart in the exam hall.", "Before your next exam, pray this verse and ask God for peace.", "What thoughts make you most anxious about exams?"),
        PlanDay("Commit Thy Works", "Proverbs", 16, 1, 3, "Thy Thoughts Shall Be Established", "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established. Committing your work to God means doing your best and leaving the outcome with Him. Your worth does not depend on your grades. Whether you pass with honours or have to resit, you are still loved by God and He still has a plan for you.", "Commit your exams and your future to God.", "How much of your worth have you placed in your results?"),
        PlanDay("Let No Man Despise Thy Youth", "1 Timothy", 4, 12, 16, "Be Thou an Example", "Paul told young Timothy, Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example. Being a student is not only preparation for later life. You can live for God now, in your words, your love and your honesty. Give attention to reading. Take heed to yourself. God can use you where you are today.", "Ask God to help you be an example to other students.", "How could you live out your faith at school or university?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_21 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "depression-and-hope",
    title = "Depression and Hope",
    topic = "Healing",
    blurb = "Ten days for low seasons, with honest prayers from Scripture and steady reasons for hope.",
    verse = "Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, who is the health of my countenance, and my God.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 42:11",
    art = Res.drawable.rhythm_reflection,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Why Art Thou Cast Down?", "Psalms", 42, 1, 11, "Deep Calleth unto Deep", "The psalmist is low. Tears have been his food day and night, and people ask, where is thy God? He does not hide it. He talks to his own soul: Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and then answers, hope thou in God. Being a believer does not make you immune to depression. You can be cast down and still hope.", "Tell God honestly how low you feel today.", "What would you say if you spoke to your own soul like this?"),
        PlanDay("Arise and Eat", "1 Kings", 19, 1, 8, "Under the Juniper Tree", "After a great victory, Elijah ran, sat under a tree and asked to die. God did not lecture him. He let him sleep, sent an angel with food, and let him sleep again. Sometimes the most spiritual thing is rest, food and care for your body. If you are struggling, please speak to a doctor or someone you trust. God works through that care too.", "Ask God for rest, and for the courage to ask for help.", "Who could you talk to honestly about how you are doing?"),
        PlanDay("How Long, O LORD?", "Psalms", 13, 1, 6, "Lighten Mine Eyes", "David asks God four times, how long? He feels forgotten. He has sorrow in his heart daily. Then in the last two verses, something turns: I have trusted in thy mercy. His circumstances have not changed yet, but he chooses to trust. You can pray honest questions. God is not offended by how long.", "Bring your how long to God today.", "What have you been waiting a long time to feel better about?"),
        PlanDay("In Darkness, in the Deeps", "Psalms", 88, 1, 9, "Mine Eye Mourneth", "This psalm has no happy ending. It is one long cry from a dark place. Yet it is in the Bible, and it begins, O LORD God of my salvation. Even in the darkness, the psalmist keeps speaking to God. If all you can do today is cry out, that is still prayer. God has made room in His word for prayers like yours.", "If you have no words, simply say, O LORD God of my salvation.", "Does it help to know that the Bible has room for your darkest feelings?"),
        PlanDay("I Will Remember", "Psalms", 77, 1, 12, "The Years of the Right Hand", "Asaph cannot sleep. He asks, Hath God forgotten to be gracious? Then he makes a choice: I will remember the works of the LORD. When your feelings say God is far away, memory can remind you that He has been faithful before. Write down times God has helped you. Read the list on the hard days.", "Write down three times God has been faithful to you.", "What has God done for you in the past that you can hold on to?"),
        PlanDay("A Bruised Reed", "Isaiah", 42, 1, 4, "He Shall Not Break", "A bruised reed shall he not break, and the smoking flax shall he not quench. A bruised reed is almost broken. Smoking flax is a wick that has nearly gone out. That is how some of us feel. God's Servant, Jesus, is gentle with exactly those people. He will not snap you or snuff you out. He handles you with care.", "Thank Jesus that He is gentle with you.", "Where do you feel bruised or close to going out?"),
        PlanDay("The Spirit of Heaviness", "Isaiah", 61, 1, 3, "The Garment of Praise", "Jesus read from this passage when He began His ministry. He came to bind up the brokenhearted and to give the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness. Heaviness is a good word for depression. Praise does not deny the heaviness. It is a garment God gives, something He puts on us, not something we have to produce alone.", "Ask God to bind up your broken heart.", "What does heaviness feel like for you?"),
        PlanDay("Troubled, Yet Not Distressed", "2 Corinthians", 4, 7, 18, "Treasure in Earthen Vessels", "Paul says, We are troubled on every side, yet not distressed; we are perplexed, but not in despair. We are cast down, but not destroyed. We are earthen vessels, cracked pots, holding a great treasure. Our weakness shows that the power is God's. though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day.", "Ask God to renew your inner self today.", "Where do you see God's strength in your weakness?"),
        PlanDay("Joy Cometh in the Morning", "Psalms", 30, 1, 5, "Weeping May Endure", "weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning. The night may be long. For some, it lasts months. But it is not forever. David had been brought up from the grave, and he sang about it. Hold on. There are people walking with you, and there is a God who has not given up on your morning.", "Ask God to bring the morning, and to help you hold on until it comes.", "What small sign of morning have you noticed lately?"),
        PlanDay("The God of Hope", "Romans", 15, 4, 13, "Abound in Hope", "Paul says the Scriptures were written so that we might have hope. Then he prays: Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing. Hope does not start with us. It comes from God, through His word and by the power of the Holy Ghost. Keep reading. Keep reaching out. He is the God of hope.", "Ask the God of hope to fill you with joy and peace.", "Which reading from these ten days gave you the most hope?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_22 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "gratitude",
    title = "Gratitude",
    topic = "Life",
    blurb = "Five days to practise thanksgiving, in good days and hard ones.",
    verse = "O give thanks unto the LORD, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.",
    verseRef = "Psalm 107:1",
    art = Res.drawable.discovery_cover_2,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Let the Redeemed Say So", "Psalms", 107, 1, 9, "He Satisfieth the Longing Soul", "Let the redeemed of the LORD say so. Thankfulness is meant to be spoken. The psalm tells of people lost, hungry and thirsty, who cried to the Lord and were led to a city. When God has helped you, say so: to Him, and to others. Gratitude spoken aloud strengthens the faith of everyone who hears it.", "Tell someone today one thing God has done for you.", "What has God done for you that you have never told anyone?"),
        PlanDay("Yet I Will Rejoice", "Habakkuk", 3, 17, 19, "Though the Fig Tree Shall Not Blossom", "Habakkuk imagines everything failing: no figs, no fruit, no flocks. Yet I will rejoice in the LORD. His gratitude does not depend on things going well. It rests on God Himself. Thanksgiving is easy when life is good. It is deepest when we thank God for who He is, even when the fields are empty.", "Thank God for who He is, whatever your circumstances.", "What would you still thank God for if everything else failed?"),
        PlanDay("His Mercy Endureth for Ever", "Psalms", 136, 1, 9, "Twenty-Six Times", "Every verse of this psalm ends the same way: for his mercy endureth for ever. It must have been sung with the people answering each line. Repetition helps truth sink in. Try writing your own version today: list what God has done, and after each one say, His mercy endureth for ever.", "Write your own thanksgiving list and answer each line with His mercy endureth for ever.", "What would be on your list?"),
        PlanDay("Remember His Marvellous Works", "1 Chronicles", 16, 8, 12, "Make Known His Deeds", "When the ark came to Jerusalem, David gave the people a song: Remember his marvellous works that he hath done. Gratitude is a kind of remembering. We forget quickly. Keeping a record, a thanks journal or a list on your phone, helps us remember what God has done and see that He is still at work.", "Start a list of things you are thankful for, and add to it each day.", "What marvellous work of God have you forgotten?"),
        PlanDay("Be Ye Thankful", "Colossians", 3, 15, 17, "Giving Thanks to God and the Father", "Paul ends a passage on living together with three words: and be ye thankful. Then he says whatever you do, do it in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks. Thankfulness is not a feeling we wait for. It is a choice, and a habit, that grows the more we practise it. Keep going after these five days.", "Ask God to make you a thankful person in every part of life.", "How will you keep practising gratitude after this plan?"),
    ),
)

private val MORE_23 = ReadingPlanDef(
    id = "the-holy-spirit",
    title = "The Holy Spirit",
    topic = "Faith",
    blurb = "Seven days on who the Holy Spirit is and what He does in the life of a believer.",
    verse = "But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth.",
    verseRef = "Acts 1:8",
    art = Res.drawable.verse_card_dawn,
    days = listOf(
        PlanDay("Another Comforter", "John", 14, 15, 26, "He Shall Teach You", "Jesus promised His disciples another Comforter, the Spirit of truth, who would be with them for ever. He would teach them and bring to their remembrance all that Jesus had said. The Holy Spirit is not a force or a feeling. He is a person, the presence of God with us, our helper and teacher. You are not left alone.", "Thank God for the gift of the Holy Spirit, and ask Him to teach you.", "What do you need the Spirit to teach you right now?"),
        PlanDay("The Day of Pentecost", "Acts", 2, 1, 13, "Every Man in His Own Language", "The Spirit came with a sound like a rushing mighty wind and tongues like fire. People from many nations heard the disciples speak of God's wonderful works in their own languages. From the start, the Spirit was for every nation and tongue. The gospel is not owned by one people or culture. It belongs to the whole world.", "Pray for the gospel to reach people in every language, including your own nation.", "How does it help to know the Spirit speaks every language?"),
        PlanDay("Abba, Father", "Romans", 8, 11, 17, "The Spirit of Adoption", "ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father. The Spirit does not make us anxious servants. He makes us children who can call God Father. The Spirit itself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are the children of God. When you doubt that you belong to God, the Spirit Himself says you do.", "Pray to God today as Abba, Father.", "When do you most doubt that you are God's child?"),
        PlanDay("The Fruit of the Spirit", "Galatians", 5, 16, 25, "Walk in the Spirit", "Paul lists what the flesh produces, and then the fruit of the Spirit: love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, meekness, temperance. Fruit grows slowly. It is not forced. If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit. Stay close to Him, and He will grow this fruit in you over time.", "Ask the Spirit to grow one of these fruits in you this week.", "Which fruit of the Spirit do you most need?"),
        PlanDay("Diversities of Gifts", "1 Corinthians", 12, 4, 11, "The Same Spirit", "There are many kinds of gifts, but the same Spirit gives them all, dividing to every man severally as he will. The gifts are given for the good of everyone, not for show. You have something to bring to the body of Christ. No gift is too small, and no one is left out.", "Ask God to show you your gifts and how to use them for others.", "What gift might the Spirit have given you to serve others?"),
        PlanDay("Strengthened with Might", "Ephesians", 3, 14, 21, "Rooted and Grounded in Love", "Paul prays that believers would be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man. The Spirit's strength helps us grasp how wide and long and deep and high the love of Christ is. Then Paul praises the God who is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think. Pray this prayer for yourself.", "Pray Ephesians 3:16-19 for yourself and someone you love.", "Where do you need strength in your inner self?"),
        PlanDay("Rivers of Living Water", "John", 7, 37, 39, "If Any Man Thirst", "On the last day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink. He spoke of the Spirit, who would flow out of believers like rivers of living water. The Spirit is not only for our own refreshment. He flows through us to others. Come to Jesus thirsty, and let Him fill you.", "Ask Jesus to fill you with His Spirit and to flow through you to others.", "Who around you is thirsty for what you have received?"),
    ),
)

